sequenceDiagram
    actor SRE
    participant ChatApp as Chat App
    participant Entra as Azure Entra ID
    participant Agent
    participant Gateway as Enterprise Agentgateway
    participant Keycloak as Keycloak (federated w/ Entra)
    participant IncidentMCP as incident-mcp (get_unhealthy_pods)
    participant RunbookMCP as runbook-mcp (get_deployment_history)
    participant RepoMCP as repo-mcp (rollback_deployment)

    Note over SRE,RepoMCP: Login (once per session)
    SRE->>ChatApp: Open chat app
    ChatApp->>Entra: OIDC authorization code redirect
    Entra->>SRE: Login prompt
    SRE->>Entra: Credentials
    Entra->>ChatApp: Entra JWT (aud=agent-gateway)

    Note over SRE,RepoMCP: Read path - stays in the Keycloak-federated home domain, silent

    SRE->>ChatApp: "Why is checkout unhealthy?"
    ChatApp->>Agent: task + Entra JWT
    Agent->>Agent: validate own Entra JWT
    Agent->>Gateway: MCP tools/call get_unhealthy_pods (Bearer Entra JWT)
    Gateway->>Gateway: validate Entra JWT (JWT auth policy, Entra JWKS)
    Gateway->>Keycloak: token exchange (subject_token=Entra JWT)
    Keycloak->>Keycloak: validate via Entra broker federation
    Keycloak->>Gateway: downscoped Keycloak JWT (aud=incident-mcp)
    Gateway->>IncidentMCP: MCP tools/call get_unhealthy_pods (Bearer Keycloak JWT)
    Note right of IncidentMCP: No JWT verification here -<br/>trusts agentgateway entirely,<br/>no tool-level gate
    IncidentMCP->>Gateway: 3 unhealthy pods, postgres connection failing
    Gateway->>Agent: result
    Agent->>ChatApp: "3 unhealthy pods failing readiness..."
    ChatApp->>SRE: shows pod status

    SRE->>ChatApp: "Show me the recent deployment"
    ChatApp->>Agent: task + Entra JWT
    Agent->>Gateway: MCP tools/call get_deployment_history (Bearer Entra JWT)
    Gateway->>Keycloak: token exchange (subject_token=Entra JWT)
    Keycloak->>Keycloak: downscope-role-enforcer caps scope to the Entra assertion's roles claim (e.g. deployment.history.read, from an Entra app-role assignment)
    Keycloak->>Gateway: downscoped Keycloak JWT (aud=runbook-mcp, scope=deployment.history.read or empty)
    Gateway->>Gateway: mcp-tool-policy CEL check (Require) - 'deployment.history.read' in jwt.roles,<br/>checked against the caller's own Entra JWT, not the downscoped Keycloak token
    alt caller has the deployment.history.read Entra role
        Gateway->>RunbookMCP: MCP tools/call get_deployment_history (Bearer Keycloak JWT)
        Note right of RunbookMCP: No JWT/role verification here<br/>either - authorization is<br/>entirely the gateway's job now
        RunbookMCP->>Gateway: checkout-api v42 (8m ago), previous v41
        Gateway->>Agent: result
        Agent->>ChatApp: "v42 deployed 8 min ago, previous v41"
        ChatApp->>SRE: shows deployment history
    else role missing (no matching Entra app-role assignment)
        Gateway->>Agent: denied by mcp-tool-policy before reaching runbook-mcp
        Agent->>ChatApp: tool call denied
        ChatApp->>SRE: shows access-denied error
    end

    Note over SRE,RepoMCP: Write path - crosses into an Entra-native domain Keycloak was never federated into

    SRE->>ChatApp: "Roll it back"
    ChatApp->>Agent: task + Entra JWT
    Agent->>Gateway: MCP tools/call rollback_deployment (Bearer Entra JWT)
    Note over Gateway: repo-mcp sits behind its own dedicated HTTPRoute, NOT covered by the shared JWT-auth policy - the Authorization header survives untouched into this exchange
    Gateway->>Entra: POST /{tenantId}/oauth2/v2.0/token - grant_type=jwt-bearer, assertion=Entra JWT, client credentials, scope=api://repo-mcp/.default
    Note over Gateway,Entra: Requires admin consent granted in advance (agentgateway app registration -> API permissions -> repo-mcp access_as_user -> Grant admin consent). No interactive popup, no banked token - a silent, direct On-Behalf-Of exchange on every request
    Entra->>Gateway: repo-mcp-scoped access token
    Gateway->>RepoMCP: MCP tools/call rollback_deployment (Bearer Entra OBO token)
    Note right of RepoMCP: No JWT/role check here.<br/>Unlike get_deployment_history, no<br/>scope-based mcp-tool-policy exists yet -<br/>gated only by Entra's admin-consent/assignment.
    RepoMCP->>Gateway: rollback successful, 5/5 healthy
    Gateway->>Agent: result
    Agent->>ChatApp: "Rollback successful, 5/5 replicas healthy"
    ChatApp->>SRE: shows confirmation
